{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>They buckle, they bow.</b> The carriers [of them]:" "<b>And could not deliver.</b> Their idols — the carried ones — for they too were taken captive. And some say that \"they buckled, they bowed\" refers to all the idols that were in Babylonia which he did not mention by name, and the idols could not rescue [their] burden, for they themselves went into exile:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:16.264904014Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}